# What NOT to upload to EAS Build.
#
# When this file exists EAS uses it INSTEAD of .gitignore, so everything that should
# stay out of the build archive has to be repeated here.
#
# google-services.json is restored from a secret rather than committed. Current EAS builds
# sync it through the GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON file environment variable; that is the
# authoritative remote-worker path. The explicit `!` rule below also includes the locally
# generated file in the upload archive when supported.
#
# google-services.json is a client-side Firebase config already embedded in the APK, so
# uploading it to the EAS builder is safe.
node_modules/
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
.DS_Store
*.log
.env
.env.local
*.jks
*.keystore
ios/
android/


# Include the Firebase client config generated by CI even though .gitignore excludes it.
!google-services.json